     2	
     3	Concrete failure scenario: this is valid YAML:
     4	
     5	```yaml
     6	verdict: GO
     7	  NO-GO
     8	release_tag: v1.3.0-rc.4
     9	```
    10	
    11	Both PyYAML and Ruby YAML resolve `verdict` as the non-authorizing scalar `GO NO-GO`. Both new shape gates, however, unconditionally ignore indented lines; both minimal parsers therefore see exactly `GO`. With an otherwise-valid envelope/delta, direct full-path probes returned server `0` and local guard `0`.
    12	
    13	The regression suite compares the two readers to each other, so this both-wrong interpretation passes its parity control. This violates the advertised exact-token and fail-closed semantics.
    14	
    15	Minimal fix: in both readers, reject any non-comment indented continuation belonging to a scalar `verdict:` declaration. Add this exact fixture to the server workflow-argv and local delta suites, requiring exit 3/E_DECISION. Keep legitimate nested lines under mapping/list fields green.
    16	
    17	The ordinary controls are genuine: rc.3 returned `0/0` for canonical NO-GO, absent, unknown, duplicate, and whitespace-key bypasses; the candidate returns `3/13`, while GO and GO-WITH-CONDITIONS remain `0/0`. Python 3.9 compilation and the stdlib-only gate passed. Full pytest execution was unavailable because the read-only sandbox provides no writable temporary directory.
    18	
    19	VERDICT: NO-GO — Both decision rails still authorize a non-authorizing valid-YAML scalar shape, so P1-4 remains incomplete.     1	No P0 findings. Two P1 defects leave the cure set incomplete.
     2	
     3	### P1 — Local decision guard accepts a valid-YAML duplicate-key override
     4	
     5	**FILE:LINE:** [.claude/scripts/local/_release_tag_guard.py:228](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc4.V1tu8w/wt/.claude/scripts/local/_release_tag_guard.py:228), [.claude/scripts/local/_release_tag_guard.py:258](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc4.V1tu8w/wt/.claude/scripts/local/_release_tag_guard.py:258)
     6	
     7	Concrete failure scenario: this valid YAML is last-wins under standard parsers:
     8	
     9	```yaml
    10	verdict : NO-GO
    11	verdict: GO
    12	```
    13	
    14	The server validator trims the key and counts two declarations. The local guard’s regex requires the colon immediately after `verdict`, so it ignores the first declaration, counts one, parses `GO`, and does not return `E_DECISION`. Thus the supposedly unconditional `release.sh tag` rail can authorize the tag.
    15	
    16	The regression controls only construct exact `verdict:` duplicates, so they do not expose the grammar mismatch.
    17	
    18	Minimal fix: make the local parser and counter use the same trimmed-key grammar as the server validator, or fail closed on noncanonical top-level key syntax. Add space-before-colon and tab-before-colon duplicate cases to both rail suites.
    19	
    20	### P1 — Night-mode delivery still fails when user ceremony already owns `.claude/.gitignore`
    21	
    22	**FILE:LINE:** [scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:858](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc4.V1tu8w/wt/scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:858), [scripts/upgrade.sh:3155](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc4.V1tu8w/wt/scripts/upgrade.sh:3155), [scripts/tests/test-night-mode-ignore-effect.sh:291](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc4.V1tu8w/wt/scripts/tests/test-night-mode-ignore-effect.sh:291)
    23	
    24	Concrete failure scenario: a user-ceremony adopter has an existing `.claude/.gitignore`, perhaps containing `/cache/`, but lacking `/state/` and `/settings.local.json`. Upgrade intentionally skips the root `.gitignore`; `_apply_claude_dir_gitignore` sees the existing nested file and returns without adding either entry. Night-mode state remains visible and commit-eligible.
    25	
    26	The positive controls use clean targets where the nested file is absent. They prove create-if-missing delivery, but not adoption over an existing user-owned file. Install/upgrade parity will also remain green because both paths preserve the same incomplete file.
    27	
    28	Minimal fix: add the two exact entries idempotently to existing nested files while preserving adopter content. Test both fresh installation and upgrade with a preseeded custom `.claude/.gitignore`, asserting custom content survives and both generated artifacts are ignored.
    29	
    30	### P2 — The documented SHA-256 regeneration command produces a SHA-1 digest
    31	
    32	**FILE:LINE:** [npm/SHA256SUMS.txt:13](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc4.V1tu8w/wt/npm/SHA256SUMS.txt:13)
    33	
    34	Concrete failure scenario: the claimed regeneration command extracts `npm pack --json`’s `.shasum`, which is npm’s legacy SHA-1 digest. It also emits no filename, so it cannot regenerate the documented `<sha256>  <filename>` manifest format. An operator following the newly qualified local-only documentation creates invalid evidence.
    35	
    36	Minimal fix: document the real local writer, or materialize the tarball and run `sha256sum`/`shasum -a 256` while emitting the filename. Add a regression assertion rejecting `.shasum` as a SHA-256 recipe.
    37	
    38	### P2 — The ceo-boot harness-probe filter suppresses unrelated real spawns
    39	
    40	**FILE:LINE:** [.claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py:516](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc4.V1tu8w/wt/.claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py:516), [.claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py:537](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc4.V1tu8w/wt/.claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py:537), [.claude/hooks/_lib/payload.py:12](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc4.V1tu8w/wt/.claude/hooks/_lib/payload.py:12)
    41	
    42	Concrete failure scenario: the filter identifies probes solely by five missing metadata fields; it never checks the probe description or prompt. `subagent_type` is optional under the payload contract. Therefore an actual event such as “Review production authentication” with those optional/derived fields absent is discarded as a harness probe, hiding precisely the unclassified spawn the ratio is intended to expose.
    43	
    44	Minimal fix: require a positive harness fingerprint—an explicit discriminator, or a tightly closed description/prompt signature. Add a negative control using an arbitrary real description with all five metadata fields absent.
    45	
    46	The npm version-neutralization, enforced/deferred contract checks, common-path checksum-honesty rewrite, and tournament working-directory patch otherwise hold. Exact-decision and clean-target night-mode controls are genuine, but miss the two P1 shapes above. Focused pytest collection was prevented by the read-only sandbox’s lack of a writable temporary directory; the findings were reproduced through direct parser/call-path probes, while syntax and repository static gates passed.
